ABILITY:Rogue Talent|TYPE:NORMAL|CATEGORY:Special Ability|KEY:Rogue Talent ~ Black Market Connections|TYPE:SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.RogueTalent.Unchained Rogue Talent|DESC:A rogue with this talent gains better access to magic items from black market connections. She treats every settlement as one size greater (see Table 15-1 on page 461 of the Core Rulebook) for the purpose of determining the gp limit of the base value of items for sale, as well as the number of minor, medium, and major magic items for sale in the settlement. If the settlement is already a metropolis, all minor and medium magic items are for sale, as well as 3d8 major magic items. With a successful Diplomacy check, the rogue can treat the settlement as two sizes larger. If the settlement is already a metropolis and she succeeds at the check, all magic items are for sale. If the settlement is already a large city and she succeeds at the check, all minor and medium magic items are for sale, as well as 3d8 major magic items. With a successful check, the rogue can also sell stolen items on the black market. If the check fails by 5 or more, the rogue does something to spook the market, and treats the city as normal for 1 week. Furthermore, those in control of the black market may alert the authorities to the rogue's presence in an act of reprisal for spooking the market or to divert attention away from their illicit activities. The DCs of the checks are by settlement size and are given in the table below.
ABILITY:Rogue Talent|TYPE:NORMAL|CATEGORY:Special Ability|KEY:Rogue Talent ~ Canny Observer|TYPE:RogueTalent.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.Unchained Rogue Talent|DESC:When a rogue with this talent makes a Perception check to hear the details of a conversation or to find concealed or secret objects (including doors and traps), she gains a +4 bonus.
ABILITY:Rogue Talent|TYPE:NORMAL|CATEGORY:Special Ability|KEY:Rogue Talent ~ Coax Information|TYPE:RogueTalent.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary|DESC:A rogue with this talent can use Bluff or Diplomacy in place of Intimidate to force an opponent to act friendly toward her.
ABILITY:Rogue Talent|TYPE:NORMAL|CATEGORY:Special Ability|KEY:Rogue Talent ~ Combat Trick|APPLIEDTO:|TYPE:RogueClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.RogueTalent|DESC:You gain a bonus combat feat.
USERPOOL:Rogue Talent|POOLPOINTS:0.0
ABILITY:Versatile Performance|TYPE:NORMAL|CATEGORY:Special Ability|KEY:Versatile Performance ~ Act|TYPE:BardClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary.VersatilePerformance|DESC:You can use your bonus in the Perform (Act) skill in place of your bonus in the Bluff or Disguise skills. When substituting in this way, you use your total Perform (Act) skill bonus, including class skill bonus, in place of your Bluff or Disguise skill bonus, whether or not you have ranks in that skill or if it is a class skill.
USERPOOL:Versatile Performance|POOLPOINTS:0.0

